    "planning_lock": "PLANNING LOCK (hard — plan OVER clusters, then write JSON):\n- Fill ALL 2 days (nights=1). No empty/partial days.\n- Mandatory destinations (preferredRegions + mustVisit): Dead Sea, Petra, Wadi Rum. Plan ONLY in these areas — any other cluster is reference material, not a day.\n- Destination→cluster map: Dead Sea→UNMAPPED (no matching cluster); Petra→UNMAPPED (no matching cluster); Wadi Rum→UNMAPPED (no matching cluster)\n- Day→cluster route (one day per cluster, in this order): D1:C0/Jerash → D2:C0/Jerash\n- mustVisit entity lock: Petra→NOT IN EVIDENCE (still plan around preferred regions); Dead Sea→NOT IN EVIDENCE (still plan around preferred regions)\n- Each day draws its POIs, meals and hotel from ITS OWN cluster.\n- No entity twice in the whole trip: a POI or restaurant used on one day cannot reappear on another, and lunch and dinner are different places. Two days in the same city are two different clusters — use each cluster's own entities.\n- Each day: 3 sights + lunch + dinner (5 entries, 6 max). Two sights only when the cluster has no third worth visiting, and say so. No gap over 90 minutes, no site under 45 minutes, at least 4 hours of sightseeing per full day.\n- activity_alternatives come from that cluster's UNUSED entities: never an entity scheduled elsewhere in the trip, and never two scheduled stops as each other's swap.\n- One visit, one fee (POIs within 600 m are parts of one site): (no such groups here)\n- Lodging requested: rating=4 star, type=boutique. Per-night base (night N = where day N ends): N1(C0): H0 [unrated] (rating absent from card — claim no rating)\n- Money: 1500 JOD covers 2 traveller(s) for 2 days (≈750 JOD/day for the whole party). Lodging = nightly rate x 1 night(s) x ~1 room(s), arithmetic shown in the notes. aiPriority=authentic → favour local, family-run entities where the cards say so. SME=Family-owned Businesses.\n- Entry fees are the last thing to cut: never skip a named destination's main ticketed site to save money, and state what is left of the budget.\n- Names/hours/fees: EntityCards only. If a card does not carry a fact (rating, booking requirement, closing day), do not state it.\n- Prices: use the card value as-is, multiplied by the party size, and show the arithmetic in the tip (\"10 JOD x 4\"). If a card has no price, estimate from pricing_level and label it \"~N JOD (estimated)\".\n- Events are reference only: never schedule them in the itinerary or budget."
  }
